# ## ChatGPT Web ###

# The `chatgptweb` provider talks to chatgpt.com through a browser-fingerprinted curl
# (`curl-impersonate`); Node's own fetch is answered with a Cloudflare 403 challenge.
# See docs/enterprise/chatgpt-web-provider.md.

# Absolute path to the curl-impersonate binary. Auto-discovered otherwise:
# PATH -> ./.cache/curl-impersonate/curl-impersonate -> /usr/local/bin/curl-impersonate (Docker image).
# CHATGPT_WEB_CURL_IMPERSONATE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/curl-impersonate

# Extra hostname suffixes appended to the transport allowlist (comma-separated); the defaults
# (chatgpt.com, openai.com, oaiusercontent.com, oaistatic.com, blob.core.windows.net) always apply.
# CHATGPT_WEB_ALLOWED_HOSTS=chatgpt-mirror.internal

# Set to '1' to let the transport talk plain http. Tests / local mock backends ONLY.
# CHATGPT_WEB_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=0

